# Frontend Development Rules - Metadata-Driven Platform

## Core Technology Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js 15+ with App Router and TypeScript 5.3+
- **Metadata Rendering**: Dynamic page generation from database metadata
- **Styling**: ALWAYS use Tailwind CSS - never write custom CSS files
- **UI Components**: shadcn/ui as base component library with metadata-driven extensions
- **State Management**: Zustand for global state, React Query for server state
- **Forms**: React Hook Form with Zod validation + metadata-driven field generation
- **Icons**: Lucide React icons consistently

## Metadata-First Architecture (MANDATORY)

- **Dynamic Pages**: All pages rendered from PageDefinitions metadata
- **Component Catalog**: Use ComponentDefinitions for all UI components
- **Runtime Forms**: Generate forms from FieldDefinitions + LayoutDefinitions
- **No Hardcoding**: Never hardcode layouts, forms, or entity structures
- **Module Manifests**: Register components via JSON manifests

## Component Strategy

- **Metadata-Driven**: Build components that accept metadata props
- **Reuse First**: Always check component catalog before creating new ones
- **Extend shadcn/ui**: Build on existing base components
- **Greek Components**: Use AFMInput, DOYSelector, GreekPhoneInput for business data
- **Extract at 2+**: If pattern repeats twice, extract to component catalog

## Dynamic Page Rendering (MANDATORY)

- **Server Components**: Fetch metadata in server components for optimal performance
- **Metadata Renderer**: Build components that render from metadata structure
- **Dynamic Sections**: Map metadata sections to UI components automatically
- **Runtime Generation**: Never hardcode page structures - always from database

## Styling Rules (MANDATORY)

- **Tailwind Only**: Never write custom CSS files or styled-components
- **Responsive**: Always include breakpoints (sm:, md:, lg:, xl:)
- **Consistent Spacing**: Use standard spacing (p-4, m-6, space-y-4)
- **Theme Colors**: Use CSS custom properties from theme metadata

## Form Standards (MANDATORY)

- **Pattern**: React Hook Form + Zod resolver + metadata-driven fields
- **Dynamic Generation**: Forms built from FieldDefinitions metadata
- **Validation**: Client-side validation with server sync
- **Component Mapping**: Map field types to UI components via metadata

- **Field Mapping**: Map field types to UI components via metadata configuration
- **Props Injection**: Pass metadata props directly to components
- **Type Resolution**: Resolve component types from field definitions automatically

## Internationalization (MANDATORY)

- **Strategy**: Database translations + JSON files for static content
- **Languages**: English (primary), Greek (business compliance)
- **Translation**: Never hardcode text - use t(labelKey) for everything
- **Metadata Keys**: All labels stored as translation keys in metadata

## Greek Business Requirements

- **Validation**: Use Greek-specific components for AFM, DOY, phone numbers
- **AADE Integration**: Include status badges and compliance indicators
- **Formatting**: Greek date, currency, address formatting
- **VAT Calculations**: Location-aware Greek VAT rates via tax engine

## Component Catalog Integration (MANDATORY)

- **Registration**: All components must be registered in ComponentDefinitions
- **Props Schema**: Define JSON schema for component props
- **Module System**: Package components in modules with manifests
- **Runtime Discovery**: Components loaded dynamically from metadata

- **JSON Manifests**: Define components in JSON with module grouping
- **Schema Validation**: Use JSON Schema for component props validation
- **Type Safety**: Ensure props match expected schema for each component

## Performance Standards

- **Metadata Caching**: Cache metadata queries with React Query
- **Component Lazy Loading**: Dynamically import components from catalog
- **Bundle Optimization**: Code splitting for module components
- **Mobile**: Mobile-first responsive design with metadata-driven layouts

## Security & Access Control

- **Permissions**: Use metadata-driven permission checks
- **Tenant Isolation**: Respect multi-tenant boundaries in all components
- **Field Security**: Hide fields based on permission metadata
- **Component Access**: Restrict component usage based on user roles

## File Organization

- **Structure**: components/dynamic/, metadata/, catalog/, shared/
- **Dynamic Components**: Components that render from metadata
- **Catalog Components**: Registered components for the platform
- **Naming**: PascalCase components, kebab-case files, camelCase hooks

## What NOT to Do

- ❌ Never hardcode page layouts or entity structures
- ❌ Don't create static forms - use metadata-driven generation
- ❌ Never write custom CSS files
- ❌ Don't hardcode text (always use metadata translation keys)
- ❌ Don't create components without registering in catalog
- ❌ Don't skip responsive design
- ❌ Don't ignore metadata validation rules
- ❌ Don't hardcode business logic - use workflow metadata

## Platform-Specific Rules

- **Keep It Simple**: Choose simplest solution that works with metadata
- **Plan First**: Show metadata approach before implementing components
- **Runtime Everything**: UI must be generated at runtime from database
- **Module Thinking**: Build reusable components for the marketplace
